// The Dual key: toggles the off hand between the dual copy and the free hand.
// Toggling back to the free hand is how you do a hands-on VR reload of the
// main gun while dual wielding, so it is bound rather than buried in a menu.
AddKeySection "Aliens VR Weapons" AEVRWeapons
AddMenuKey "Dual wield on/off" ae_dualkey
alias ae_dualkey "netevent ae_dual"

// 2026-10-22 (owner: "need a keybind for dual like BD22"): bound out of the box to the off
// controller's X button (free in QuestZDoom's default layout: A use, Y jump, B free, X free).
// Rebind under Customize Controls -> Aliens VR Weapons.
defaultbind Pad_X ae_dualkey
// RESET THE HAND SLIDERS, 2026-10-24. The hand placement is hook + slider ADDED
// (zscript/rsq/hands.zs:150): "the owner tunes in the headset and bakes the numbers into
// GunHook afterwards". So baking a fitted hook is one step with two halves -- set the
// hook AND clear the slider that was standing in for it -- and doing only the first
// moves the hand by the sum of both. This is the second half, in one command, so the
// two can happen together instead of one of them being forgotten.
//   ae_hands_reset        every hand slider back to 0
alias ae_hands_reset "ae_gunhand_fwd 0; ae_gunhand_side 0; ae_gunhand_up 0; ae_knifehand_fwd 0; ae_knifehand_side 0; ae_knifehand_up 0; ae_pistolhand_fwd 0; ae_pistolhand_side 0; ae_pistolhand_up 0; ae_satchelhand_fwd 0; ae_satchelhand_side 0; ae_satchelhand_up 0; ae_smarthand_fwd 0; ae_smarthand_side 0; ae_smarthand_up 0; ae_support_gun_fwd 0; ae_support_gun_side 0; ae_support_gun_up 0; ae_support_pistol_fwd 0; ae_support_pistol_side 0; ae_support_pistol_up 0; ae_support_smart_fwd 0; ae_support_smart_side 0; ae_support_smart_up 0"
